  "problem": {
    "statement": "The parent (abel-ruffini-oq-04-oq-01) proved Gal(x⁵ - 4x + 2) ≅ S₅ and asked whether x⁵ - x - 1 is a second concrete S₅ witness, claiming it could be handled 'by the same argument used here' after a sign analysis showing '3 real roots'.",
    "goal": "Determine whether the parent's complex-conjugation argument transfers to x⁵ - x - 1, and machine-check the elementary facts a correct S₅ proof would reuse."
